   "evidence": "Both proofs build the same family `F`, the same `hz`/`hqn` bounds, `Summable.of_norm_bounded` with `summable_geometric_of_lt_one(...).mul_of_nonneg`, the same `hcol` via `hasSum_geometric_of_norm_lt_one`, and the same `prod_fiberwise` closing step. The only difference is the coefficient bound; `hasSum_lambert` uses `Nat.norm_cast_le` with `hasSum_coe_mul_geometric_of_norm_lt_one`. The ultrametric section exists only to provide `norm_natCast_le_one` for `hc`.",
